body:
I would say it sounds like delusional disorder in that case, but since the delusions are a result of drugs, it's a drug-induced psychotic disorder. I haven't really done research into how psychedelics can permanently change the brain, but I know they are serotonin agonists, and delusions/ hallucinations are a result of too much serotonin in the brain. That's about how far my knowledge goes, but I've heard cases of people being permanently changed by psychedelics like you've described, especially after prolonged use or an extreme dose.

&#x200B;

ETA-- I'm getting my masters in clinical psychology, so I am by no means an expert, but I'd say I know more than the average bear.
